== Where does this come from? ==
Two sources, and it is worth knowing which is which:

* '''The change list''' comes from [https://freebuff-changelog.nordicnode.workers.dev/ an unofficial changelog] that reads the public code repository [https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff CodebuffAI/freebuff] and summarises every commit. It is '''not written by Freebuff staff'''. The commits are real; a one-line summary of a commit can still put the emphasis in the wrong place. That is exactly why every entry links to the commit itself.
* '''The blog posts''' come from the official feed [https://freebuff.com/blog/rss.xml freebuff.com/blog/rss.xml].

The official [https://freebuff.com/changelog Freebuff changelog page] exists, but its newest entry is 18 August 2026, so it cannot be used for a "what's new" list. It is still the right place to read polished release notes for older months.

